WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.516
Hey! Welcome to a new season of Project Kamp, number 3!

00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:08.065
We have many cool things planned for this year!

00:00:08.065 --> 00:00:10.424
We already have the people here!

00:00:10.424 --> 00:00:12.159
New projects coming up!

00:00:12.159 --> 00:00:15.574
But, in this video, we're going to show you 
some things we did this winter...

00:00:15.574 --> 00:00:17.847
Some upgrades we made, some improvements, so...

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.097
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:20.097 --> 00:00:22.592
So, this winter, it was actually super rainy...

00:00:22.592 --> 00:00:26.903
Here is a graph from the internet, where you can see
the amount of rainfall, in the last 10 years.

00:00:26.903 --> 00:00:28.501
So, there was really a spike this year...

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:31.069
And, we thought Season 1 had a lot of rain!

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:35.569
So, one big thing I learned this week, 
is that it actually rains quite a lot around here...

00:00:35.708 --> 00:00:38.003
But, actually, this year was even more...

00:00:38.031 --> 00:00:40.801
But, to be fair, you do notice it a bit less now.

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.728
Because, we had a house,
 where it was nice and warm, and dry.

00:00:43.728 --> 00:00:46.970
And, we had a waterfall we could look at,
which was cool with all the rain.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:51.377
But, it still does have a few downsides, 
living in shipping containers, and in vans.

00:00:51.377 --> 00:00:54.491
So, let me show you a few of those winter downsides.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.114
So, winter in the van can be a bit rough...

00:00:57.114 --> 00:01:00.199
But, not because of the cold,
 but of the rain and humidity.

00:01:00.975 --> 00:01:02.580
So, we needed some upgrades.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.326
And, first, it's really nice to have some dry area outside.

00:01:06.326 --> 00:01:09.349
So, you can leave your shoes outside, 
without getting it full of rain.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.101
And, second, it wears out the vans, 
especially if they're under all this rain...

00:01:14.101 --> 00:01:17.169
Mine was getting rusty, and some painful leaks we're appearing...

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.937
It's intense being outside all the time, so I wanted to make a big cover,
 before the intense winter started.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.754
Got some tubes, connectors, a big tarp...

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:29.629
Some rope...

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.218
And, anchors.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:33.555
Time to set it up!

00:02:55.473 --> 00:02:57.499
Let me also give you an update on the waterfall.

00:02:57.499 --> 00:03:01.240
So, at the end of last season, 
we repaired the water gate at the lagoon.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.727
And, we got to test it, with the first rainfall.

00:03:03.727 --> 00:03:08.338
But, during winter, it became an awesome landscape,
with more than 12 waterfalls altogether.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.049
A lot of rain has fell!

00:03:10.049 --> 00:03:14.243
So, I want to show you what
 the waterfall looks like now, after a bit of rain.

00:03:38.668 --> 00:03:41.392
A really fun place to be in winter, with all this energy flowing...

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.602
So, we continued to work a bit there...

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.485
Aiming to have a nice place, 
where we can be in summer.

00:03:46.485 --> 00:03:49.219
Cleaning the area around it up a bit more...

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:53.148
Cutting a big, old, burnt chestnut...

00:03:53.148 --> 00:03:54.960
It burned to death from a recent fire.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:59.628
Chopped it into smaller pieces, 
so we can use it as firewood in the house...

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:05.468
Also, started cleaning up the terraces,
that were originally there, and planted some grass.

00:04:06.243 --> 00:04:08.813
Hoping this would be a nice place to sit in summer.

00:04:09.506 --> 00:04:12.318
Also, moved some of the big rocks around...

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.240
To improve the flow, and clear everything out of the water.

00:04:20.644 --> 00:04:24.853
And, it's really nice to use these big amounts of water, 
that are coming in to clear everything up.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:32.751
And, also, repaired the small wooden gate,
that controls the water flow on the right top side.

00:04:35.716 --> 00:04:40.622
It's pretty cool to use this water system, that was originally there, 
and play with the different dams, and openings.

00:04:47.051 --> 00:04:50.529
And, this is what it looks like now, in spring time, after winter.

00:04:51.665 --> 00:04:53.638
The grass has already grown pretty well.

00:04:53.638 --> 00:04:56.013
Seems like we could use this in summer, huh?

00:05:05.731 --> 00:05:09.667
So, all this water flowing here, is the same water,
that flows in the creek on our land.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:13.571
So, here are some updates from Julie, 
to see how it's going down the stream.

00:05:13.668 --> 00:05:15.295
So, here we are at the creek!

00:05:15.295 --> 00:05:19.407
After a nice rainy winter, we have the creek flowing again!

00:05:34.756 --> 00:05:38.522
So, by being so close to the creek,
we also make use of it, and plant some fruit trees.

00:05:38.522 --> 00:05:42.133
Now, in spring time, there are some new leaves coming!

00:05:47.281 --> 00:05:49.900
Okay, so, last year, we have been clearing quite a bit of the creek.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:53.958
Unfortunately, we noticed that it was too big
 of a job for one season...

00:05:53.958 --> 00:05:55.911
So, we continue on this, this year.

00:05:56.354 --> 00:05:59.764
You can see here it here: one big pile of old brambals from last year.

00:06:00.983 --> 00:06:04.587
But, as you see close by, the new ones are already coming back...

00:06:04.587 --> 00:06:06.384
Nature is taking over.

00:06:06.384 --> 00:06:08.328
The creek was not the only thing we cleared, last year.

00:06:08.328 --> 00:06:09.690
Let's have a look at the well!

00:06:22.258 --> 00:06:24.925
So, last year, we placed a piece of the old shower, 
on top of the well.

00:06:24.925 --> 00:06:28.156
Just making sure that the animals don't fall into the well...

00:06:28.655 --> 00:06:30.159
Or, a human...

00:06:36.634 --> 00:06:41.433
As you might remember from last year, 
we were scooping out the bottom layer of the well.

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:44.859
At the moment, there is quite a lot of water in the well!

00:06:44.859 --> 00:06:47.853
This year, we're going to keep an eye on it,
and see how it reacts...

00:06:50.763 --> 00:06:51.917
-A small fish?

00:06:51.917 --> 00:06:53.339
No! It has four legs!

00:06:53.339 --> 00:06:54.599
Maybe, it's a salamander?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.714
- Nice!

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:02.301
Enough about the well now!

00:07:02.301 --> 00:07:05.067
Let me close this up with the old shower...

00:07:06.619 --> 00:07:08.443
And, let's give you a bit on the new shower!

00:07:11.878 --> 00:07:13.268
So, here we are at the new shower!

00:07:13.268 --> 00:07:17.012
We added a little door, so the privacy is even better.

00:07:17.012 --> 00:07:19.103
To be not as exposed as we were before...

00:07:19.629 --> 00:07:21.184
Let's have a look inside!

00:07:23.674 --> 00:07:25.177
So, here we are, at the bottom of the shower.

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:26.584
Let's see how the basin is doing!

00:07:27.249 --> 00:07:30.966
Wait, so, some extra information, 
why we are having a look at the bottom.

00:07:30.966 --> 00:07:33.857
This basin is part of a research we did last year.

00:07:33.857 --> 00:07:35.467
Trying a new type of cement...

00:07:35.467 --> 00:07:41.966
It's experimental, so I wanted to show you what it 
looks like, after an intense winter, and some months of usage.

00:07:45.255 --> 00:07:45.895
So...

00:07:46.421 --> 00:07:47.265
No cracks!

00:07:47.265 --> 00:07:48.166
It's all looking good!

00:07:48.692 --> 00:07:50.740
A bit dirty, but it is what it is.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.712
Water flows away easily, and no stops during winter

00:07:56.652 --> 00:07:58.884
So, the shower has been behaving quite well!

00:07:58.884 --> 00:08:01.884
The only thing that we see,
is that there is some mold appearing.

00:08:01.884 --> 00:08:03.055
Have a closer look.

00:08:03.055 --> 00:08:07.289
So, it's red cider with linseed oil, 
but it's getting a bit moldy...

00:08:07.871 --> 00:08:10.667
So, the wood is very interesting how it reacts during winter...

00:08:10.667 --> 00:08:12.336
But, Adrian will tell you more about that!

00:08:13.361 --> 00:08:18.178
Last year, as you might have noticed, we built three yoga decks,
 in three different places of the land.

00:08:18.178 --> 00:08:22.871
We used three different kind of wood,
to check what behaves better.

00:08:22.871 --> 00:08:25.863
This is a yoga deck made out of eucalyptus.

00:08:25.863 --> 00:08:28.901
A tree that you can find everywhere around!

00:08:28.901 --> 00:08:30.957
It became very dark now...

00:08:31.524 --> 00:08:36.868
It's in a shady place, very close to the swamp.

00:08:36.868 --> 00:08:42.603
What happens with the eucalyptus sometimes,
is that it cracks, and moves a bit more than the other wood.

00:08:43.046 --> 00:08:45.053
But, still behaving..

00:08:45.718 --> 00:08:47.635
So, we're on the top platform!

00:08:47.635 --> 00:08:51.390
This is made with pine wood,
 and protected with linseed oil.

00:08:52.304 --> 00:08:55.654
It's very exposed to the sun, to the wind, to the rain...

00:08:55.654 --> 00:09:01.210
So, even in the same spot, you can find different results, 
depending if it's exposed to the sun, or not.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.814
If it dries or not...

00:09:03.814 --> 00:09:05.764
And, if it doesn't dry, it gets mold...

00:09:05.764 --> 00:09:07.101
If it dries, it loses the color...

00:09:07.627 --> 00:09:11.346
So, here you can see it's way more moldy than in the top.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.203
So, it's a little challenge to try to avoid the more chemical products.

00:09:16.203 --> 00:09:19.154
Like, the varnishes, and these kind of things...

00:09:19.154 --> 00:09:25.341
And, try to use only natural materials,
and natural products like linseed oil.

00:09:26.588 --> 00:09:30.772
It's a matter of testing, balancing, and checking what's better.

00:09:30.772 --> 00:09:34.442
We're in the bottom of the land, at the bottom deck now.

00:09:34.442 --> 00:09:37.419
This is built with red cedar on the top.

00:09:37.419 --> 00:09:41.488
It's protected with an artificial oil.

00:09:41.488 --> 00:09:46.693
This used to be the product we used, 
for the first structures we have made in Basekamp.

00:09:46.693 --> 00:09:51.552
For the floor, it's very good protected, and it's using red cedar.

00:09:51.552 --> 00:09:53.092
As you can see!

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:58.230
Even, if it's exposed to the sun, 
to the rain, and it's close to the creek...

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.789
Which, makes the place a bit humid.

00:10:00.789 --> 00:10:04.059
It's perfect in it's state, like the first day.

00:10:04.059 --> 00:10:07.026
You can see that we treat the top with this product...

00:10:07.026 --> 00:10:08.734
But, on the bottom, we let it grow.

00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:11.557
The result of the red cedar is quite good!

00:10:11.557 --> 00:10:15.838
It's a wood that is very suitable for being outside.

00:10:15.838 --> 00:10:21.299
Because, even if it's raw: no mold, straight, no cracks...

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:25.438
It's a bit soft maybe, sometimes for some uses...

00:10:25.438 --> 00:10:28.862
But, so far so good!

00:10:28.862 --> 00:10:30.758
We are now in Basekamp.

00:10:30.758 --> 00:10:32.192
Let me show you a funny fact!

00:10:32.691 --> 00:10:35.845
So here, we have a funny roundabout.

00:10:36.538 --> 00:10:37.916
Of course, the other way around...

00:10:37.916 --> 00:10:40.346
Made out of red cedar, during Season 2.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:46.131
Not a single protection, but all clean, and mold safe!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.863
Funny to see! Let's see!

00:10:52.715 --> 00:10:54.681
We are now in the Basekamp structures.

00:10:54.681 --> 00:10:57.464
This is pizza hut we built, during Season 1.

00:10:57.464 --> 00:10:59.204
We oiled it with linseed oil.

00:11:00.067 --> 00:11:05.815
We re-oiled it at the end of Season 2 again, 
but still, you can see it's full of mold...

00:11:05.815 --> 00:11:09.079
it's getting a bit ugly with this color covering...

00:11:09.079 --> 00:11:12.434
Black dots, some white parts...

00:11:13.537 --> 00:11:17.171
We are still looking for a nice way, to protect our structures.

00:11:17.171 --> 00:11:19.367
We still didn't find a way...

00:11:19.367 --> 00:11:23.029
But, we keep on working on it!

00:11:23.029 --> 00:11:25.597
Last thing, I wanted to show is our pizza oven.

00:11:25.597 --> 00:11:28.527
So, from the beginning, it started to have some cracks...

00:11:28.527 --> 00:11:33.230
We think that is, because of the expansion, 
and the contraction of the metal door.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:35.869
So, it creates this crack in the front.

00:11:35.869 --> 00:11:40.282
But, with the time, it went a bit too crazy...

00:11:41.751 --> 00:11:44.273
So, we are losing some parts...

00:11:44.273 --> 00:11:47.286
At some point, we had some leaks in some parts of it too...

00:11:47.286 --> 00:11:52.763
Under the oven, there's something that made us 
quite worried at some point...

00:11:52.763 --> 00:11:56.016
I feel that now it's still standing okay, but...

00:11:56.016 --> 00:11:59.252
It start to heat up a bit too much, 
at the bottom of the oven...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.754
So, it got a bit burnt...

00:12:02.754 --> 00:12:05.287
But, still working good!

00:12:05.287 --> 00:12:10.505
Doesn't need to do much, besides putting wood, 
keep the heat, and then we bake...

00:12:10.505 --> 00:12:14.738
Pizzas are still tasty, and the bread is 
getting tastier and tastier too!

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.542
So, yeah...

00:12:19.567 --> 00:12:20.640
So far so good!

00:12:21.748 --> 00:12:24.792
So, these were some updates of things,
 that were happening in the winter...

00:12:24.792 --> 00:12:29.189
But, there's also some stuff to prepare, 
before the people are coming for the new season...

00:12:29.189 --> 00:12:32.305
And, the first one, is to get our workspace up and running.

00:12:34.032 --> 00:12:37.532
So, currently in the workspace, we're gonna tidy it up a bit.

00:12:37.532 --> 00:12:38.697
But, also, re-stock...

00:12:38.697 --> 00:12:41.035
Some things are missing, like this screwdriver.

00:12:41.668 --> 00:12:45.878
Filling up the screw system, and making sure 
all the paint is back in stock...

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:48.627
So, making sure it's ready, for new people to come!

00:12:50.179 --> 00:12:54.518
Many different kinds of paint, and we need to get paint system...

00:12:54.518 --> 00:12:56.249
It's a mess.

00:13:22.536 --> 00:13:25.197
It's a bit messy, but slowly, we're getting there!

00:13:25.613 --> 00:13:27.539
We need to repair some tools.

00:13:27.539 --> 00:13:31.108
Also, some things are broken, like cables that got ripped.

00:13:31.108 --> 00:13:36.570
Safety glasses: some are broken, some are a bit wore out...

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:39.238
This doesn't work -- no trust...

00:13:39.986 --> 00:13:43.497
So, we also have a bunch of drills that got bland...

00:13:43.497 --> 00:13:46.874
We don't want to use them again...

00:13:46.874 --> 00:13:48.077
We could sharpen them by hand.

00:13:48.077 --> 00:13:52.295
But, we know that it's a difficult process, 
to sharpen them by hand, on the grinder...

00:13:52.988 --> 00:13:58.681
So, if you have any solution, or any nice sharpener, 
that we could install here potentially, just let us know.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:47.747
Okay, so, next: we have a rougher situation, 
that shows the real side of winter here.

00:14:47.747 --> 00:14:48.935
- A lot of rain!

00:14:48.935 --> 00:14:52.114
Please stop eating, and finish your drink, before we move on...

00:14:52.434 --> 00:14:56.196
So, before winter came, we made sure everything was stored dry.

00:14:56.196 --> 00:14:59.580
And, we thought that would be enough, 
to keep things safe...

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.434
But, apparently not...

00:15:01.434 --> 00:15:03.322
Not for Mr. Mold.

00:15:03.322 --> 00:15:08.201
So, for instance: here you can see a cabinet, 
under the roof, getting all moldy...

00:15:08.201 --> 00:15:10.811
The handle of the pizza oven got all moldy...

00:15:10.811 --> 00:15:13.470
Some wooden spoons in the kitchen...

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:17.791
And, especially textured surfaces, even more, like this glove...

00:15:18.234 --> 00:15:21.619
It was pretty rough, seeing this happen over winter, with all our stuff...

00:15:21.619 --> 00:15:25.700
And, the humidity also affected some of our metal structures...

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:30.688
They got rust on top, and we all just noticed that some mice 
were walking around in the kitchen...

00:15:31.685 --> 00:15:37.935
So, yeah, time for a deep spring cleaning
and repair upgrade job to the kitchen.

00:16:03.197 --> 00:16:06.431
So, we just dismantle everything, and take everything
out

00:16:06.431 --> 00:16:13.685
We really go into the very moldy corners, 
and a lot of mice flew around...

00:16:13.685 --> 00:16:16.207
We put everything out...

00:16:19.492 --> 00:16:20.877
And, we clean it.

00:16:22.153 --> 00:16:23.520
- Spring cleaning?

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:24.696
Spring cleaning...

00:16:44.334 --> 00:16:50.122
So, we're currently repainting some of 
our metal structures, that are in the kitchen.

00:16:50.122 --> 00:16:55.235
Like the cabinet, and stuff, 
because they got a bit rusty in the winter.

00:16:55.235 --> 00:16:56.670
And, just after using them...

00:16:59.375 --> 00:17:00.842
So, some maintenance...

00:17:16.922 --> 00:17:19.124
Look at this brand new shelf!

00:17:35.134 --> 00:17:39.003
Last season, we finished most of 
the renovation of our small ruin.

00:17:39.774 --> 00:17:42.200
The long-term goal is to use it as a guest house.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:46.054
But, until it's ready, we use it for whatever is most needed.

00:17:46.054 --> 00:17:48.461
So, it was awesome for winter, for example...

00:17:48.461 --> 00:17:51.355
No mold here, just comfort and heat.

00:17:51.601 --> 00:17:55.188
And, for the coming season, we want to use it as an office.

00:17:55.188 --> 00:18:00.237
So, we have a proper space to work on the computers,
 video editing, and so on...

00:18:00.237 --> 00:18:02.560
- Make a short video
each week to keep the algorithm happy...

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:10.156
I mean, Basekamp is okay, but it can get annoying 
to do computer stuff, with the heat, the rain, the flies...

00:18:10.156 --> 00:18:10.945
- Damn flies...

00:18:10.945 --> 00:18:12.721
And, the noise that happens all around...

00:18:15.719 --> 00:18:17.914
And, we actually already have a big table!

00:18:17.914 --> 00:18:21.562
You might have seen us taking it out of 
the container in Season 1.

00:18:22.034 --> 00:18:23.849
It was very heavy!

00:18:23.849 --> 00:18:26.088
Made of an old bowling track.

00:18:26.088 --> 00:18:30.840
And, we thought of putting that into the ruin, 
which will become an office.

00:18:31.533 --> 00:18:34.169
We also have with it: a big mess...

00:18:34.169 --> 00:18:38.233
We have to take everything out!

00:18:38.233 --> 00:18:42.320
So, that we can pull the bowling table, 
and we can paint it back a bit...

00:18:43.013 --> 00:18:44.615
And, use it for the office.

00:19:19.052 --> 00:19:20.753
Now, it's all rusty... 

00:20:43.539 --> 00:20:45.358
So, now, the table is ready!

00:20:45.358 --> 00:20:49.167
All painted, and all clear...

00:20:49.167 --> 00:20:52.310
It's ready to go down, which will be a big task!

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:55.818
Because, not only is it super long, but it's also super heavy...

00:20:55.818 --> 00:21:02.203
Which, means that we will have to take
the table all the way around the roads...

00:21:04.032 --> 00:21:06.978
And then, the table is four meters.

00:21:07.366 --> 00:21:12.561
It means that we have to do some funky angles, 
 in order to put it through that door, into the house.

00:21:13.143 --> 00:21:17.356
Which, means that we have to take down a few of these mimosas...

00:21:17.356 --> 00:21:22.570
It's kind of a pity, because they are quite of 
a chunky tree, and giving a good shade.

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:27.671
But also, they are, according to regulations, 
too close to the house, so it's also good to take them down.

00:21:27.671 --> 00:21:32.066
So, this afternoon, Jan will be chopping down some mimosas.

00:21:32.066 --> 00:21:35.360
So, that we can go to the next step, of bringing the table.

00:21:35.681 --> 00:21:37.428
- I'm ready!

00:22:12.656 --> 00:22:17.308
So, we assembled a big team, to move a big table.

00:22:17.308 --> 00:22:21.263
It would be a funny task, 
and we are not sure we will make it...

00:24:00.691 --> 00:24:03.844
Make sure the wood is underneath, Julie, 
when we put it down there.

00:24:07.383 --> 00:24:08.604
- Pull this one!

00:24:09.182 --> 00:24:10.259
Completely, yeah?

00:24:10.536 --> 00:24:11.708
- Enough?

00:24:11.847 --> 00:24:14.400
That the wooden top hits it...

00:24:14.899 --> 00:24:16.154
- Okay...

00:24:16.154 --> 00:24:17.190
Okay, good!

00:24:17.799 --> 00:24:18.795
- It's gonna break!

00:24:18.795 --> 00:24:19.967
The woods breaking!

00:24:20.189 --> 00:24:21.495
- Which one?

00:24:22.686 --> 00:24:24.455
This board, here?

00:24:27.364 --> 00:24:32.937
- Now, we're in the air...

00:24:36.234 --> 00:24:37.871
Okay, now, you need to pivot...

00:24:40.197 --> 00:24:41.247
It fits!

00:24:45.570 --> 00:24:47.192
- Pivot on here, but don't slide!

00:24:49.908 --> 00:24:51.469
Adrian, the back comes to me.

00:25:56.400 --> 00:25:57.356
We managed.

00:25:57.356 --> 00:26:01.106
Kind of a hard task, but now we just need the easy parts...

00:26:01.106 --> 00:26:09.143
Which, is just putting some storage space,
chairs, and turning this place into a proper office. 

00:26:19.090 --> 00:26:24.100
At this point, we are almost ready for the season to start,
and have the people come in.

00:26:24.100 --> 00:26:28.255
This year, we are going to be with more,
at the same time in Project Kamp.

00:26:28.255 --> 00:26:30.860
Last season, the maximum was 15.

00:26:30.860 --> 00:26:34.953
This year, we will go up to 25, 
but the peak will be around summer.

00:26:35.535 --> 00:26:38.215
For now, we have the first new campers arriving!

00:26:38.215 --> 00:26:41.940
They come from different parts of the world,
 with different skills and backgrounds.

00:26:43.048 --> 00:26:45.141
Many of them come with their vans.

00:26:45.141 --> 00:26:47.471
Quite a coincidence that hey are all white...

00:26:47.471 --> 00:26:49.443
And, some others will stay in tents.

00:26:50.108 --> 00:26:53.770
For this, we still needed to brush cut the area, 
and set up the tents itself.

00:26:54.795 --> 00:26:57.620
But, with them around, it was a super fast action.

00:26:57.620 --> 00:26:59.806
And, we could do it in a couple of hours!

00:27:04.382 --> 00:27:07.790
Okay, one last thing we wanted to do was weeding the garden...

00:27:08.372 --> 00:27:12.601
Last season, it was nice and tidy, 
and was a source for nice herbs and teas.

00:27:13.634 --> 00:27:16.719
But, over the winter, it got completely overgrown.

00:27:16.719 --> 00:27:20.279
Weeds took over the place, 
and many plants froze and died.

00:27:20.944 --> 00:27:25.083
We kind of like the wild look, 
but it can easily get out of control.

00:27:25.083 --> 00:27:27.860
And weeds don't let other desired species grow.

00:27:29.301 --> 00:27:34.756
Okay, so, we will now transform 
this winter garden, into a spring garden.

00:27:51.024 --> 00:27:55.800
So, we worked hard on it, because we wanted
to have it ready, before the people come.

00:28:07.104 --> 00:28:09.535
But actually we didn't manage to finish it on time...

00:28:11.198 --> 00:28:16.748
And anyway, now we are with more people, 
it's a less challenging task, and we can do it super fast!

00:28:16.970 --> 00:28:17.747
Yeah!!!

00:28:51.105 --> 00:28:53.572
All right, so, that was it! 
The Kamp is now ready!

00:28:53.572 --> 00:28:55.963
The people are here... 
Time to take on new projects!

00:28:55.963 --> 00:28:59.796
In the next video, we're actually going to 
show you all the things we're going to do in the next season.

00:29:00.322 --> 00:29:03.008
If you already want to see that video, 
make sure to support us on Patreon!

00:29:03.008 --> 00:29:05.168
If not, we'll just see you again, next week!

00:29:05.168 --> 00:29:06.594
Same time! Same channel!

